{"step_index":67,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-20T07:31:50Z","content":"Created At: 2026-11-20T10:31:50+03:00\nCompleted At: 2026-11-20T10:31:53+03:00\nCreated At: 2026-11-20T10:31:50+03:00\nCompleted At: 2026-11-20T10:31:53+03:00\nThe search for \"\"hyprland.lua\" \"source\" OR \"require\" site:wiki.hypr.land\" returned the following summary:\nAs documented on the Hyprland Wiki, starting with version 0.55, Hyprland has transitioned from the legacy `hyprlang` syntax (`hyprland.conf`) to a Lua-based configuration system centered around **`hyprland.lua`**[1][2]. \n\nBecause the configuration is a standard Lua file typically located at `~/.config/hypr/hyprland.lua`, you are not forced to put everything into a single massive file[1]. You can split your configuration into multiple separate modules/files and import or load them using Lua's built-in **`require()`** function[1].\n\n### Modularizing your `hyprland.lua` Configuration\n\nYou can structure your configuration directory like this:\n```text\n~/.config/hypr/\n├── hyprland.lua\n└── configs/\n    ├── env.lua\n    ├── keybinds.lua\n    ├── monitors.lua\n    └── windowrule.lua\n```\n\nInside your main `~/.config/hypr/hyprland.lua`, you can pull in these modular files using standard Lua `require`:\n\n```lua\n-- ~/.config/hypr/hyprland.lua\n\nrequire(\"configs.env\")\nrequire(\"configs.monitors\")\nrequire(\"configs.keybinds\")\nrequire(\"configs.windowrule\")\n\n-- Global configuration table using the hl API\nhl.config({\n    general = {\n        gaps_in = 5,\n        gaps_out = 10,\n        border_size = 2,\n        resize_on_border = true,\n        layout = \"dwindle\",\n    },\n    decoration = {\n        rounding = 10,\n    },\n})\n```\n\n### Best Practices & Order of Execution\n* **Load Order Matters:** Ensure that environment or utility modules (`require`) are loaded before any other modules that rely on those states or call specific `hl.*` functions[3].\n* **File Paths:** Lua’s `require` looks for modules relative to your Lua search paths, or you can require them using relative paths/dot notation depending on how you structure your config directory tree.\n\nSources:\n[1] [archlinux.org](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFRfkvz6r2r0mph9mscG2bXeVqsk9_5O_dZ-BqvmCICGAvmDvX9LzcYyWZnLXejrLMVr6D3XlYpfXpekZPK09MOAC1aok_d8D8A8FvL3tGw7qSS6Q5Wdfe_-dI0Z12bqQ==)\n[2] [wikipedia.org](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGaTuyM4SDuaQRuQ0lw6R4ewO5lTIgTAxgNcuFZcXgmq9NPVQRVS1SRHEQNBLv0zbhoOL9O8eZjPpcVi4HXAcxloJESkIu6Q7SLQQBaGKPn-MCKLwBxQr4YcUSxTg==)\n[3] [hyprflux.dev](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGS-GXqD5K8EuQS5iFZn-4RN1GQV3C7ARMQg-0wbBA3u7h5eh70quGTADUorWqT-kUeLxelf_xrQGsBE-TjaAsI7pPCWqapywzIWR_xs6nyy83qBUSZJmL-)\n\nNote: Source URLs are HTTP redirects; check where they resolve if you need the direct link."}
