{"step_index":71,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-20T07:32:03Z","model":"gemini-3.8-flash-medium","input_tokens":2687,"cache_read_tokens":51463,"output_tokens":802,"thinking":"The configuration uses shell variables within Lua. The suspicion is that these variables are not directly accessible in the Lua context. There is a need to load the color definitions from the shell configuration file into Lua. A simple Lua helper function will be created to read and parse the color file to resolve this.\n\n\nCreated a Lua function to load and parse color definitions from the WAL configuration file, defaulting to fallback colors if the file is absent. Examined Hyprland's configuration to confirm color definitions are accepted in the correct format, specifically for active and inactive borders. Additionally, verified shadow colors can be set using the same color variables.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"grep -n -C 5 \"shadow\\.color\" /usr/share/hypr/stubs/hl.meta.lua","WaitMsBeforeAsync":5000,"toolSummary":"Search shadow.color type"}}]}
