{"step_index":73,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-20T07:32:12Z","model":"gemini-3.8-flash-medium","input_tokens":3309,"cache_read_tokens":52116,"output_tokens":876,"thinking":"The color property supports both strings and gradients, so the original color value is compatible. The user's configuration file will be examined line-by-line. The color sources will be checked first, then the monitor settings. The goal is to identify possible configuration errors in the user's setup.\n\n\nThe monitor configuration utilizes \"preferred\" mode and \"auto\" scale. Examining `/usr/share/hypr/hyprland.lua` confirms this, also showing scale can be numeric or a string. The autostart configuration employs `exec-once` which requires further verification of its Lua implementation.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"search_web","args":{"query":"\"hl.exec_cmd\" \"rules\" hyprland site:wiki.hypr.land OR site:github.com"}}]}
{"step_index":74,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-20T07:32:20Z","content":"Created At: 2026-11-20T10:32:20+03:00\nCompleted At: 2026-11-20T10:32:24+03:00\nCreated At: 2026-11-20T10:32:20+03:00\nCompleted At: 2026-11-20T10:32:24+03:00\nThe search for \"\"hl.exec_cmd\" \"rules\" hyprland site:wiki.hypr.land OR site:github.com\" returned the following summary:\nIn Hyprland's Lua-based configuration system (introduced in version 0.55), **`hl.exec_cmd(cmd, rules)`** (and its dispatcher equivalent **`hl.dsp.exec_cmd(cmd, rules)`**) allows you to execute a shell command while optionally passing a table of window rule effects/parameters to apply to the spawned process[1][2].\n\n### Overview\n\n* **Syntax:** `hl.exec_cmd(\"command\", { rules })` or `hl.dsp.exec_cmd(\"command\", { rules })`[1]\n* **Behavior:** It spawns an asynchronous process (using `sh -c`)[1][3]. Unlike the legacy `exec-once` syntax from `hyprlang`, you do not need trailing `& disown` characters[4][3]. \n* **Rules Parameter:** The second argument takes a table of window rule properties/effects to target the resulting window directly[1].\n\n---\n\n### Examples\n\n#### 1. Launching an app on a specific workspace (Silently)\nIn the Lua configuration, rules like workspace placement can be supplied directly inside the execution command wrapper[5]:\n\n```lua\nhl.on(\"hyprland.start\", function()\n    -- Launch Thunderbird on workspace 2 silently\n    hl.exec_cmd(\"thunderbird\", { workspace = \"2 silent\" })\nend)\n```\n\n#### 2. Keybindings with `hl.dsp.exec_cmd`\nWhen binding commands to key combinations, you can pass rules or flags to format how the window behaves upon launch[5]:\n\n```lua\n-- Open a floating window with specific dimensions and placement on a workspace via keybind\nhl.bind(\"SUPER + SHIFT + W\", hl.dsp.exec_cmd(\"librewolf --new-window https://www.youtube.com\", { \n    workspace = \"6 silent\", \n    float = true, \n    size = { 1275, 1383 }, \n    move = { 1279, 199 } \n}))\n```\n\n*(Note: Depending on how quickly asynchronous apps like Electron/GTK applications start up and request focus, some users manage complex layout positioning via standard global `hl.window_rule` definitions matched by application class, as process-tracking rules via `exec_cmd` can occasionally vary based on application PID behavior)[4][6].*\n\nSources:\n[1] [hypr.land](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQH0sQHbmLJmYTRS5lZWnNLgLxhAa25f7cWJiAyA0gjkQtM0F_Lh7YFBhM9Oy-nw1zqfj93JjVsc0dHpiU5AhR5pDMAl5_wszvW-0FhjZLE5dXP4RHPHVsaGS1WB-H_3qbABVwQ4sA4HPF6u)\n[2] [wikipedia.org](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFEesuoSGlYr4MX7wv5k6CgywSNIPLltfoFwm5fgwVWA_wEhSEh7xIutr5mN_T2IPQmvyE2U8u2mrrXnS24JC8YDNvJSO4noL0Wxtr9LYMv0JKbmBFvgAn7lxu34A==)\n[3] [hypr.land](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFe1uW9hNCDKxTzK7SWIuFwyDM0pf4871FpzaGazwSIR5pdmbachKpzs6BIKnwMeqfO3MeFAH1MtnyUxuqrY_U7zyBzptUnBuAykf8r_jNzO_28SLMj5bXduB4tmV105lGEmm5CK8ubARvsQKvF7zRW7g==)\n[4] [github.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQHwL-6EyKlvvrPmIg6QVKwakl3AeNFKKnq5a13vvel_ESg0e4A290Mc2K_2OSrTddJqrItXW5xD7ANK2drlXEAGUZomkI5PBWzoX7Euru-b7oUV5iE_j2Z38A9w9wjP2PvSBAK1w6AnLq4n)\n[5] [reddit.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGmkNwZMh715Zn8GNWIrZK_UyeEPriIUD5U3zZMSMyhOH2GGJGCIETkwUbZ_Uac-DgFBa2-aUe8GkfQ0XnLxSy3NhMrAqH9DoskaJ4zKxYn5vwzACtP6wqeTPJqRySE1ZXl8QmA-GFOOyeVIonHQqQI7cMgevyS15appAqzbMWgBAq6semRtywXTTNdJw1QBXLB7lOMNOLC)\n[6] [reddit.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQEBOQXESe6TwBv2v5PCIaC8GrQp7YaeMU6CQqvDliQMDy60SifMcmCkmppWAhYCX9lP4P5A-dE0cBjMQ6kxWj1cJ_Ov99cS8Tuqjr2xy9XbKK1-8_qzcZngdJUKG5PC12Qk9SsQFvhk6cHE1s_4CgzpQ5OAJSrvoqlLh0zgl9OVnMkr6B52DJ9LNGYL)\n\nNote: Source URLs are HTTP redirects; check where they resolve if you need the direct link."}
